{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And HaShem commanded me, etc. to teach you statutes and judgments.</b> These are the rest of the commandments of the Torah that He was commanded at Sinai, apart from the Ten Statements that were on the tablets. Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״ואותי צוה ה׳״ — this refers to the Oral Torah." "<b>That you may do them in the land.</b> Not that they are not a bodily obligation in every place, but to teach that the essential performance of the commandments is in the land, for they are the judgment of the El of the land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:17.245758276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}